{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408956-why-isn-t-there-a-tv-show-about-vampire-the-masquerade","id":1408956,"title":"Why isn't there a tv show about vampire the masquerade?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-18T09:45:35-07:00","id":1408956,"title":"Why isn't there a tv show about vampire the masquerade?","content":"Paradox mentioned, when they first purchased White Wolf, that they wanted to have a Netflix like show based on this IP. So why hasn't it happend yet? Vampires are popular right? Maybe not as much as a couple of years, when several vampire tv shows were on the air, but people still like them.<br /> <br /> AMC recently bought The Vampire Chronicles from Anne Rice. So that's getting made. But still no word on a show based on The World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Streaming services like Netflix make a lot of shit show's. So why not make a show about an ip that has a loyal followers base? Based on a popular genre (Vampires).<br /> <br /> Not to mention the amount of written material that they could use. I just can't wrap my head around the fact that we still don't have a proper tv show based on this universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 08-18-2020, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T10:45:03-07:00","id":1408972,"title":"","content":"For the same reason that no one ever did a remake of Ishtar or Waterworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T10:57:32-07:00","id":1408973,"title":"","content":"There was, Kindred: The Embraced. Aaron Spelling produced it, the show was absolutely terrible and took huge liberties with the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0115232/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0115232/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0115232/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0115232/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T11:16:36-07:00","id":1408977,"title":"","content":"Have you watched What we do in the shadows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T12:03:21-07:00","id":1408983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408956-why-isn-t-there-a-tv-show-about-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1408977#post1408977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you watched What we do in the shadows?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have and i like it but i would like my vampire shows to be a bit more serious. I am a fan of the earlier seasons of True Blood and even The Originals/Vampire Diaries. I think a vampire show set in the World of Darkness made today could trump any vampire show that came before. There is a lot of potential with this franchise that has not come to fruition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 08-18-2020, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T12:11:12-07:00","id":1408984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408956-why-isn-t-there-a-tv-show-about-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1408973#post1408973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was, Kindred: The Embraced. Aaron Spelling produced it, the show was absolutely terrible and took huge liberties with the setting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0115232/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0115232/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Best not to talk about that abomination <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T12:28:19-07:00","id":1408985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408956-why-isn-t-there-a-tv-show-about-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1408984#post1408984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Best not to talk about that abomination <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, ya it was pretty awful. I do like the actor that played the Brujah Primogen, Brian Thompson. Kelly Rutherford without the Southern accent she used in Brisco County Jr feels weird, though. It's an odd collection of the character actors from mid '90s Fox. The only reason to watch it is for the same reason people go to car races just to see a wreck.<br /> <br /> Not a TV series and not specifically the same universe Masquerade takes place in, but Only Lovers Left Alive is an awesome, recent vampire flick by Jim Jarmusch. It is so Toreador. What We Do In The Shadows references it with Tilda Swinton running the vampire council, so that was the vampire flick she was in that got her in that scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T14:04:51-07:00","id":1409001,"title":"","content":"I found K:tE to be rather entertaining, but I also consider <i>The Room</i> to be the closest thing this world has to an objective masterpiece (as everyone who watches it has a great time)<br /> <br /> My guess: A variety of factors:<br /> V5 is controversial and removes the strong themes that really held a lot of the TV-series appeal. The 90's nostalgia is in right now, but that'd drive up costs. <br /> Way too many characters, and some of them aren't supposed to age. Yet a narrow focus would confuse people<br /> It'd be expensive in effects. Especially if they did anything with werewolf. <br /> <br /> <br /> It'd be fucking miserable, and pretty damn funny if you wanted to do it right. <br /> Personally, I'd go a whole half season or so before it's even revealed that some of the characters are vampires, and I'd introduce werewolves by following a kid just before his first change, where he slaughters his classroom (a great way to end the first season) You need that kind of slow burn to introduce the setting. But also a producer would make this really difficult to do. Especially when you wanna make political statements (A whole load of incompetent, trigger happy, nasty police) . <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T14:11:09-07:00","id":1409003,"title":"","content":"Honestly, you could tell True Blood's writers were straight up cribbling from V:TM in the final seasons when Lilith and the Book of Nod showed up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T14:11:43-07:00","id":1409004,"title":"","content":"If you squint a little, there have actually been quite a few successful vampire shows in the last decade. Vampire Diaries and the spin of the originals, if you take out the high school drama and ignore some of the less reputable actors was all together not terrible. True Blood was decent if you ignore certain parts like Were-panthers. The Immortals is actually quite amazing if you can deal with sub-titles. Dracula was short, but well produced with some great actors. Being human (BBC version) was actually quite good. The strain was ok, though its more of a zombie apocalypse then a vampire show. The Gates was mostly terrible but I liked the idea of it and of course From Dusk Till Dawn is kind of like a show where you know vampires exist but don't really interact with them.<br /> <br /> Not saying any of them where great, I mean realistically if you un-squint, they where all quite terrible, but this may very well be a pretty good reason not to get into the vampire show business, given that in the last 20 years the most successful show about Vampires has been Buffy the Vampire Slayer. The genre doesn't have a particularly great track record of success and seems to generally do better in the movies than in TV shows, though I would argue that both True Blood, Vampire Diaries and The Originals where successful shows that showcase that it is indeed possible to make money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24511-xguild","name":"xguild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T14:33:52-07:00","id":1409011,"title":"","content":"I'll always love &quot;Kindred: The Embraced&quot; for the daffy decision to make the Ventrue prince the sympathetic lead character and his Brujah rival the heavy. It was a night time soap opera, so naturally the rich and powerful were the good guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T14:58:09-07:00","id":1409016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408956-why-isn-t-there-a-tv-show-about-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1409011#post1409011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll always love &quot;Kindred: The Embraced&quot; for the daffy decision to make the Ventrue prince the sympathetic lead character and his Brujah rival the heavy. It was a night time soap opera, so naturally the rich and powerful were the good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much describes anything done by Aaron Spelling. Hard to believe they guy who made Melrose Place and Beverly Hills 90210 did K:TE.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T15:05:41-07:00","id":1409019,"title":"","content":"You can't tell me the Immortals wasn't someone's Turkish players' V:TM LARP. It is the most 90s show I have ever seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T16:43:38-07:00","id":1409035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1408956-why-isn-t-there-a-tv-show-about-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1408984#post1408984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Best not to talk about that abomination <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.co